From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 21:56:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 40/63] fix(github-pr-review): abort the comment steps when the
 review scope fails (gcp-m7dn)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous commit gives run-review a real failure path, but a failed step
alone does not stop this adapter. The four review/comment steps were chained
with `needs` only, and `needs` is a READINESS edge, not an OUTCOME edge: once
run-review CLOSES — pass or fail — render-comment, human-gate-comment and
post-comment all become Ready and the run posts a verdict for a review that
never succeeded. Detection without propagation would still put the comment on
the pull request.

graph.v2 ships the mechanism for exactly this. Marking the four steps
`gc.scope_ref`/`gc.scope_role=member` with `gc.on_fail = "abort_scope"` and
adding a `review-scope` body makes the orchestrator skip the remaining OPEN
members and close the body `gc.outcome=fail` when any member fails
(formula-spec-v2 section 3.5, implemented at
internal/dispatch/runtime.go:reconcileTerminalScopedMember). finalize moves onto
the body rather than post-comment so it still runs on the aborted path and
records why — it is deliberately NOT a member, since a member would be skipped
by the very abort it needs to describe.

This wiring is not new code so much as relocated code: it has been running as a
whole-file city-local fork of this formula since gc-kvqb, whose own header says
it "belongs upstream — retire this fork the moment upstream carries it". The
committed file is byte-identical to that fork apart from two deliberate
differences: the `code_review_formula` default stays `review` here (moving it to
`verdict-review` is gc-6l2k, a separate concern that depends on a formula this
pack does not ship), and the scope body gets a `description_file`, which this
pack's own test_formula_node_descriptions_delegate_to_shadowable_assets requires
of every node.

The selector-matrix test built its route map by indexing `gc.run_target` on
every step, which KeyErrors on a latch step that has none. It now uses a
worker_run_targets() helper that skips orchestrator-closed steps, which is the
correct reading: latches are not routed to a worker.

Validation: new test_github_pr_review_scopes_comment_steps_so_a_failed_review_aborts
pins the member/body/finalize wiring. `gc lint gascity` is clean and the full
`pytest tests gascity/tests` run is back to exactly the four failures that a
clean checkout already has (test_no_bare_bd_commands and three
test_city_claim_command_* subtests, all untouched by this branch).
